            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0383" n="279" xml:id="pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/65: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru (Dearing) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-15T21:00:00-05:00">September 15,
                            1932—9 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 15—8:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>167. Department’s 55, September 15, 12 A.M., just received. I am glad to report I
                    have followed exactly the lines indicated in these instructions in my
                    conversations here. While the Department’s message is stated to be for my
                    personal information I believe it will be advantageous to communicate it orally
                    and informally to Foreign Minister and will do so unless Department deems it
                    inexpedient.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
